# Alembic revisions land here.
#
# There is deliberately no initial revision checked in. Generate it against a
# real PostgreSQL instance:
#
#     docker compose up -d db
#     alembic revision --autogenerate -m "initial schema"
#     alembic upgrade head
#
# Autogenerate reads the DDL dialect from the database it is connected to, so a
# revision generated against SQLite would emit SQLite types (no JSONB, no
# TIMESTAMPTZ) and then fail or silently degrade on Postgres. Generating it
# against the real target is the only way to get it right.
#
# For a fresh install you do not need migrations at all — db/schema.sql is
# applied automatically by docker-compose on first start.
